# Kubernetes contexts of the exam environment. Like the real exam, every question starts
# with "Set configuration context: kubectl config use-context <name>", and clusters differ.
#
#   <context>   <cluster>
#
# Cluster 1 is k3d "ckad" (1 control plane + 1 worker): the Ingress, NodePort, node and
# image questions live there. Cluster 2 is k3d "ckad2" (1 node). Each question names its
# context in questions/qNN/context; the runner sets up and grades a question in that context
# whatever the terminal's current context is, so work done in the wrong cluster scores 0.
# Without a second cluster (no /ckad-state/kubeconfig-2), every context points to cluster 1.
ckad-c1   1
ckad-c2   2
